{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#137","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#137","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#137\",\"parent_revision\":\"37263684021c4a35068b4d81c36cbafd072809c7d7b67abd3d0e3ab218daca6b\",\"root_revision\":\"37263684021c4a35068b4d81c36cbafd072809c7d7b67abd3d0e3ab218daca6b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`skilllint --record` emits SVG with trailing whitespace. The `trailing-whitespace` prek hook then strips it, so anyone regenerating a screenshot gets a CI failure on their first push.\\n\\nThis already happened once this session, on #105's `docs/screenshots/rules.svg` regeneration.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA `.rstrip()` in the record path.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #131 \u2014 screenshots are committed build outputs with no regenerator; this trap sits directly in the path that issue proposes to automate\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"41d7fd26fdbb5ae73d45359ecfc03691399607d9070161bb631c7f6f443ca916\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-OTg\"}"}